@startuml
title Rebar AutoDim — Revit API Interaction Sequence

actor "Structural Engineer" as User
participant "Rebar AutoDim" as Plugin
participant "Active View" as View
participant "Area Reinforcement" as Area
participant "Structural Grids" as Grids
participant "Revit Document API" as Doc
participant "Generation Metadata" as Meta

User -> Plugin : Run command

Plugin -> View : Read active view context
View --> Plugin : Origin, directions, scale, crop

Plugin -> Area : Collect visible Area Reinforcement
Area --> Plugin : Candidate zones

Plugin -> Grids : Collect visible structural grids
Grids --> Plugin : Grid geometry and references

loop For each supported zone

    Plugin -> Meta : Read previous generation metadata
    Meta --> Plugin : Previous generated result ID / none

    alt Previous result exists
        Plugin -> Doc : Start transaction
        Plugin -> Doc : Delete previous generated result
        Doc --> Plugin : Deleted
    else No previous result
        Plugin -> Doc : Start transaction
    end

    Plugin -> Area : Read boundary geometry
    Area --> Plugin : Boundary curves / geometry

    Plugin -> Plugin : Project geometry to view coordinates
    Plugin -> Plugin : Build normalized rectangle
    Plugin -> Plugin : Resolve nearest grids
    Plugin -> Plugin : Calculate dimension placement

    Plugin -> Doc : Create supporting detail curves
    Doc --> Plugin : Stable references

    Plugin -> Doc : Create overall dimensions
    Doc --> Plugin : Dimension elements

    Plugin -> Doc : Create grid offset dimensions
    Doc --> Plugin : Dimension elements

    Plugin -> Doc : Create generated group
    Doc --> Plugin : Group ID

    Plugin -> Meta : Store group reference
    Meta --> Plugin : Metadata updated

    Plugin -> Doc : Commit transaction
    Doc --> Plugin : Commit result

end

Plugin --> User : Report processing result
User -> Doc : Review generated annotations

@enduml